my name is julie i am the director at  lux bag spa here at lux bag spa we  restore luxury designer handbags i'm  going to show you how we are going to  restore this very loved chanel handbag  this is a chanel classic flap and it's  about 12 to 15 years old a bag like this  the state that it's in it would be about  fifteen hundred dollars after the  restoration it could go to about five or  six thousand usd the bag definitely  needs a really good clean we're gonna do  a full coloration as well as take the  strap apart and make sure we're  polishing all of the hardware  this bag looks to have many years of  dirt and grime build up on it  first we're gonna go ahead and clean the  exterior of the bag just with a gentle  mild leather cleaner using a horsehair  brush this really helps get into the  leather and the cracks of where the  stitching is so we're able to really get  a deep clean without hurting any of the  exterior leather  i'm going to go in now with our leather  moisturizing cream i want to use this  actually before i start pigmenting the  back because i don't want the bag to  crack so i will just let this sit on for  a little bit  it has avocado oil in it so it will  bring back a lot of its original  moisture  now we've unraveled the entire chain and  the reason that we're doing this is  because we want to polish the hardware  separately from it being attached to the  leather of the chain  we're going to go in with the same  leather cleaning solution that we did  for the exterior of the bag and we're  going to also use the gentle horse hair  brush  now that we've finished cleaning i'm  going to go in with a acetone based  leather primer so we want to take off  even more pigment if we are able to  just to make sure that the bag is  prepped and ready for the coloration  looking in the interior you can see that  there is some of the original color  still in here so this is actually what  we're going to be color matching in the  bag  i'm going to go in with a small angled  brush just so i have more control over  concealing these areas i like to think  of the bags as how you would do your  makeup you want to conceal the darker  spots first before applying the rest of  the pigment this just makes it more  cohesive throughout and makes the bag  look like it did as the original  i'm switching now to a larger paintbrush  when we're doing the full exterior  coloration this just helps me cover more  surface area of the bag and really get  into those grooves  i am painting this bag by hand because i  find i have a lot more control  i'm going to apply filler to this area  here to make it smooth on this interior  flap  after the filler is completely dry we  want to go in with a sander we just want  to make sure that everything is level  and just looks natural on this flap  as you can see here i have left the  panel surrounding the cc without any  pigment and you can already see the  color difference between the two but the  reason we're doing this is because we  don't want the silver polish to destroy  or deteriorate any of the pigment that  we're going to put on now since it is  quite a harsh chemical so i go into all  the hardware with a q-tip just dipping  it into the silver polish and rubbing  away any tarnish or dirt that has  collected over the years  i'm going in with an angled brush that i  also used for concealing this bag  i just want to be a little bit more  precise with  painting around the cc and if i got any  pigment on the cc it doesn't really  matter i'm able to take a q-tip and wipe  that right off but i try and keep it as  clean as possible  now i'm going to go in with the second  layer and i'm doing this a little bit  thinner than the one prior  now we're going to look at doing  coloration on the strap here we're going  to go in and conceal the dark marks just  like we did on the exterior of the full  bag and then go in and paint the  entirety of the strap  even though we did polish the entirety  of this chain there is a few spots that  we want to resell our plate for these  spots here we will use our  silver plating tool which we dip into a  solution and with electromagnets it  actually puts silver back onto where  it's scratched off or tarnished off over  time  now that the strap is completely dry  we're going to weave it back together  when doing this we want to make sure  that the strap is completely straight  and if it isn't then your chanel bag is  going to be turning in a whole bunch of  different directions so this is a really  important step  using the same leather solution that we  did on the exterior i'm going to go in  with a horse hair brush and clean the  inside here  luckily we were able to get the interior  quite clean so this won't have to be  repigmented now we're going to apply our  top coat for this particular bag i chose  a matte topcoat and this actually will  lock in all the pigment that we  previously put on  i am super excited with how this  restoration turned out and i'm so  excited to see how the client likes it  when she receives her bag  [Music]
 

